# Investment & Compliance Limits — TokenRealty

Human doc: [docs/rules/investment-limits.md](../../docs/rules/investment-limits.md).

Adapted from Titan limits engine — **no Redis Lua / card velocity engine**. TokenRealty uses compliance checks + listing rules + future policy service.

## What we skip from Titan

- `limits-service`, Redis atomic counters, ISO8583 decline codes (61/65/57)
- Per-card daily/monthly velocity, MCC/country blocks on auth hot path

## What we use instead

| Concern | Where | Mechanism |
|---------|-------|-----------|
| KYC / whitelist | Token Issuance | `GET /v1/compliance/check/{wallet}` before order match |
| Min investment | Marketplace listing | `minInvestmentTokens` on `Listing` |
| Token availability | Marketplace | `tokensAvailable` decrement on match |
| Compliance block | Payment (future) | Re-check wallet before escrow release |
| Jurisdiction (future) | Compliance Service (:8087) | Country rules → whitelist sync |

## Evaluation order (marketplace buy flow)

1. Listing active + sufficient `tokensAvailable`
2. `tokenAmount >= listing.minInvestmentTokens`
3. KYC check via `TokenIssuanceClient.checkWallet(buyerWallet)` — fail → 422 `ComplianceBlockedException`
4. Order match → `PaymentClient.initiateTokenPurchase` (escrow + `trade.paymentId`)
5. Payment confirm (`POST …/confirm` or dev auto-confirm) → `payment.confirmed` → Issuance transfer → `transfer.completed` → settle + `PaymentClient.releaseEscrow`

Evaluate compliance **before** creating matched order / holding escrow. Escrow release only after on-chain transfer confirmed (via `transfer.completed` event).

## Rules

- Never hardcode bypass of KYC in production paths — use service token + compliance API.
- Listing min/max investment belongs on `Listing` entity — not ad-hoc controller checks.
- Decline with typed exceptions (`ValidationException`, `ComplianceBlockedException`) — not generic 500.
- Idempotent reversal: cancel order → restore `tokensAvailable`; release escrow via Payment API.

## Future Compliance Service

When `compliance-service` exists:

- Centralize KYC status, jurisdiction rules, accredited-investor flags
- Token Issuance keeps whitelist sync; Marketplace/Payment call Compliance port
- Policy changes via DB — not hardcoded in Marketplace service

## Payment limits (future)

- Max single payment amount per profile (config or compliance policy)
- Payout batch size limits for dividend distribution
- Require `Idempotency-Key` on payment POST — see [payment-ledger.mdc](payment-ledger.mdc)

